#: includes/Privacy.php:57
msgid "Flinkform — Form Submissions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Privacy.php:59
msgid ""
"When a visitor submits a form built with Flinkform, the plugin stores the "
"submitted field values (name, email, message, etc.) in a dedicated database "
"table on this website. No IP addresses or browser user-agent strings are "
"collected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Privacy.php:61
msgid ""
"Submissions are retained until a site administrator deletes them "
"(individually or in bulk), until the plugin is uninstalled, or — when a per-"
"form retention period is configured — until they are older than that period,"
" after which a daily routine deletes them automatically."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Privacy.php:63
msgid ""
"Flinkform does not send any submission data to external services. (Add-ons "
"such as Flinkform Pro may add integrations — e.g. webhooks or SMTP delivery "
"— that transmit data to third parties; those add their own privacy "
"disclosures when active.)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Privacy.php:65
msgid ""
"The built-in spam protection (proof-of-work challenge) runs entirely in the "
"visitor's browser and on this server — no data is sent to any external anti-"
"spam service."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Privacy.php:67
msgid ""
"Flinkform sets one short-lived, strictly necessary cookie "
"(\"flinkform_flash\", lifetime ~60 seconds, httpOnly) — and only when a "
"submission fails validation, to carry the error message across the page "
"reload. No tracking, analytics or marketing cookies are ever set."
msgstr ""

